{"title":"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a certain sequence of numbers, the first number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39abfe232e2ed5247aa4028089e5f651090e66da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, the product of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> numbers in the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />. \nThe sum of the third and the fifth numbers in the sequence is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/f/d7ff9c06d5cd8ccd5a4484d354b1b50a0f8e72eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{25}{9}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{31}{15}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{61}{16}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{576}{225}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"423\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution by e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p>Since the product of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> numbers in the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, the product of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> numbers in the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57efb5c0b218135087ac110b8467426b528d7856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" />. Therefore the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />th number in the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85de036d68e68f6d1dd147e52ba24713ab281cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(n+1)^2}{n^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore the third and the fifth numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b033d87594e25926781185595ecc09bf7577209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/658d34fe4c66abc876b78ad047b34566b2d8360a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> respectively. The sum of those numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a5b14974d221400de3fe6da735c6c43ff437b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36}{16}+\\frac{25}{16} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{61}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"159\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME\" title=\"1979 AHSME\">1979 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1979 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Pr